@nsobid-FF773E90972D544EB79406EAA65396D53C43EFB9

# Super Mario Bros. Wonder 1.2.1 - Disable anti-aliasing

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables every post-process anti-aliasing pass.
//
// All of the game's AA is agl::pfx::FilterAA, drawn at the end of the gsys
// final-image pass (sub_710015EA50). It dispatches on antialias_type: 0 = FXAA
// (with history reprojection), 1 = ReduceAA, 2 = SMAA, 3 = a draw callback.
//
// Whether the filter runs at all is one test in that pass: the scene allows AA,
// the filter's scale is above zero, and the filter is enabled. When it fails,
// the pass resolves the scene buffer straight to the final target, the same
// path a scene with the filter switched off takes. The test now always fails,
// so no AA mode runs whatever antialias_type, enable flag or scale a scene or
// environment file sets.

@enabled
0015EE10 07060014   // B to the AA-off result (was LDR S0,[X5,#0x2838] = FilterAA scale)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Super Mario Bros. Wonder 1.2.1 (sead +
// agl/gsys ModuleSystem, NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; the site
// was located by structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being
// written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
